  "dependency_note": "Every local net keeps at least one global name tag: KiCad names the net after it, which the netlist gates against the live model and the frozen V2 netlist (bare V2 net names) rely on; a local net gets a second tag only where the planner repeats the name at a far-away pin or replaces a long / looping wire by a tag pair.  single_global_labels counts the global labels whose name occurs exactly once in the project: each one is a warning of KiCad's single_global_label ERC check, which is ignored by default and is not part of the ERC gate (0 findings with --severity-all).  four_way_junctions counts points where four wires meet (one junction dot, two nets would be unreadable there): the planner itself only draws T-joins, the sheet router may land a fourth leg on an existing junction of the same net, so a non-zero count is a reading-ambiguity figure, not a connectivity error.",
  "definitions": "One definition for every generator version: the V2 release sheets (releases/v2/kicad/<board>) and the V2.1\nsheets are parsed with native_schematic.parse and measured alike, so before/after comparisons are honest.",
  "board": "control"
